Package: retort
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, ffmpeg
Recommends: retort-cli
Suggests: vainfo, vulkan-tools
Description: Convert video and audio files with FFmpeg
 Retort converts any audio or video file into any format FFmpeg can write,
 with simple presets ("MP4 that plays everywhere", "Fit under 10 MB", …) and
 an advanced mode that exposes almost every FFmpeg option.
 .
 Hardware acceleration (NVENC, VA-API, Quick Sync, Vulkan, AMF, V4L2) is used
 only where a real test encode proved it works on this computer, with an
 automatic fallback to software.

Package: retort-cli
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, ffmpeg
Description: Convert video and audio files with FFmpeg (command line)
 retort-cli is the headless companion of Retort: system check, hardware
 probing, format listing and batch conversion with the same presets and the
 same verified hardware acceleration. It has no GTK dependency, so it suits
 servers.
